  {
    "client_msg_id": "1b1418a1-8acb-4101-a7a7-78055381f21e",
    "type": "message",
    "user": "U08RZQ547LJ",
    "text": "\u003e • Any reason why we are not allowing numbers in the catalog name?\n\u003e • The info box says if catalog name left empty, it will default to olake_iceberg, but the box is a required field\nHey \u003c@U0ACFDEBBQB\u003e, both of these issues have been fixed in our new release, *OLake-UI v0.4.9*.\n\nIf you're using Helm, please redeploy your Helm release to pick up the latest changes.\n\nEDIT: If you're using the _latest_ image tag with Helm, you can simply delete the OLake UI pod and Kubernetes will recreate it with the latest image.",
    "ts": "1784003552.959999",
    "thread_ts": "1782902467.145229",
